{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 22, :comments ["<b>From the blood that is in the basin.</b> That there be a dipping upon every sprinkling, as the El commanded in saying <b>upon the two doorposts</b> — and this first, and afterward upon the lintel — and this is impossible save with three dippings. This alludes to the three yods, as the Sages said: \"The World to Come was created with a yod\" — and so it was before the sin of the first Adam and on the day of the giving of Torah until the calf, for in them יהוה צור עולמים (Isaiah 26:4) are eternal. For the yod indicates the simplicity of the eternal, and the supernal yod indicates the existence of the singular in His world upon two eternal worlds." "<b>And you shall not go out.</b> Behold, the house shall be marked with blood, and you shall not go out, and in this manner — and He passed over — in the manner of וְהִתְוִיתָ תָּו (Ezekiel 9:4)."], :book :exodus, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 12, :notes {0 "I read שָׁלוֹשׁ הַזָּאוֹת as 'three dippings/sprinklings' parallel to the three applications of blood; the closing phrase עַל שְׁנֵי עוֹלָמִים is rendered hyper-literally as it stands."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:25:13.947075366Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}